From: ManicardiMatteo87 <manicardi.matteo87@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:26:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 14/19] diag(build): name the composition of the P5 diagnostic
 in BuildConfig

82c1af9 (validated on the fixture on 16/11, the best timing measured on the chip)
plus P5 (87338f8 on research/p0-stopplan-20261116, cherry-picked unchanged). P4 is
left out: on the chip the attenuated releases that overrun still took two solves.
Still a diagnostic build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 05_Firmware/MATDOG_Controller/src/config/BuildConfig.h | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/05_Firmware/MATDOG_Controller/src/config/BuildConfig.h b/05_Firmware/MATDOG_Controller/src/config/BuildConfig.h
index d2c05a8..35e7b84 100644
--- a/05_Firmware/MATDOG_Controller/src/config/BuildConfig.h
+++ b/05_Firmware/MATDOG_Controller/src/config/BuildConfig.h
@@ -163,6 +163,10 @@ constexpr const char* kFirmwareDescription = "Embedded Motion & Robot Control Fi
 //   plus the accepted offset), P3a (bit-identical ViaPlan::plan), P3b (plan
 //   release keeps the probe) and D3 (last release lost with Motion idle, the
 //   @MOTION TIMING dump duration, the register-85 pass duration).
+// P5 diagnostic (composed 2026-11-16 on 82c1af9, the best timing measured on the
+//   chip; P4 left out, no gain on the overrun releases): plus P5, a refused STOP
+//   proof stops at the first duration with a control outside the box (same
+//   accept/refuse, same plans). Still diagnostic.
 constexpr const char* kFirmwareVersion = "1.0.2-dev.8"; // P0 diagnostic build only; not an operational candidate
 constexpr const char* kBoardName       = "YD-ESP32-S3 N16R8";
 constexpr const char* kBuildId         = MATDOG_BUILD_ID;
